= Predictability: Does the Flap of a Butterfly's Wings in Brazil Set Off a Tornado in Texas? / 可预测性：巴西蝴蝶扇动翅膀，会在得克萨斯引发龙卷风吗？

#html.p(id: "en-G001")[#text("The title presents a question about sensitivity: can extremely small differences between weather states grow into substantially different outcomes? A vivid image introduces a problem of prediction.")]

#zh(id: "G001")[#text("题目提出的是一个关于敏感性的问题：天气状态之间极小的差异，能否发展成明显不同的结果？一个生动的意象引出了预测问题。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G002")[#text("Lorenz separates the evolution of a system from our ability to specify its starting state. Deterministic rules need not make long-range forecasts practically reliable.")]

#zh(id: "G002")[#text("洛伦兹把系统怎样演变，与我们能否准确确定它的初始状态区分开来。即使规则是确定的，长期预测也未必在实践中可靠。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G003")[#text("Avoid reading the title as a demonstrated causal history of one butterfly and one tornado. The lecture asks how perturbations affect possibilities and the limits of forecasting.")]

#zh(id: "G003")[#text("不宜把题目读成已经证明的、某一只蝴蝶导致某一次龙卷风的故事。演讲讨论的是扰动怎样影响可能的结果，以及预测的限度。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G004")[#text("Reading question: how much uncertainty in an initial measurement can a prediction tolerate? Think about this before equating a better model with an unlimited forecast horizon.")]

#zh(id: "G004")[#text("阅读时可以追问：一个预测能容忍多大的初始测量误差？在把更好的模型等同于无限长的预测期限之前，先想想这个问题。")]
